#
# rcraid auto-bind rules, X399 (1st/2nd-gen Threadripper) — generated by the
# rcraid installer.
#
# On X399 the array members keep their native NVMe vendor/device IDs, so
# there is nothing on the PCI device to match.  Instead the installer
# recorded the PCI address of every drive that carried AMD RAIDCore metadata
# at install time, and each rule below fires when the stock nvme driver
# exposes that drive's namespace.  rcraid-bind then re-reads the RAIDCore
# block from the namespace and only hands the PCI function to rcbottom if it
# is still there — a different drive moved into a member's slot stays on
# nvme.
#
# Re-run the installer if you move, add, or replace array drives.

@MEMBER_RULES@
